==Significant policies and initiatives==
===Agriculture===
*Easing restrictions on gas and methane emissions from pastoral farming.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending|pending implementation}}
*Reverse the ban on live animal exports.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Introduce legislation easing restrictions on genetic engineering.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Reforming the membership, mandate and function of the National Animal Welfare Advisory Committee.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Halting the review of the [[New Zealand Emissions Trading Scheme]].<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}} 
*Incentivising emissions reduction mitigations such as low methane genetics and animal feed.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}} 
*Encouraging government agencies to use woolen fibres at government buildings.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}

===Constitutional===
*Introduce legislation on a referendum to extend the parliamentary term to four years.<ref name=newshub-election /><ref>{{cite news |title=National on promise to introduce legislation on extending parliamentary term to four years: 'It will save money' |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/political/503268/national-on-promise-to-introduce-legislation-on-extending-parliamentary-term-to-four-years-it-will-save-money |access-date=18 July 2024 |work=[[RNZ]] |date=26 November 2023 |language=en-nz}}</ref> {{efn|name=pending}}

===Education===
*Shifting the "Fees Free Scheme" from the first year to final year of tertiary study. (came into effect Jan 1 2025)<ref name="1 News new govt" /><ref name="RNZ 24 Nov 2023" /><ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Eliminating all references to gender, sexuality and "relationship-based education guidelines" in educational curriculums.<ref name="RNZ 24 Nov 2023" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Requiring schools to institute one hour of reading, writing, and mathematics each day.<ref name="RNZ 24 Nov 2023" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Reintroducing [[Charter schools in New Zealand|charter schools]] and allowing state schools to convert to charter schools.<ref name="RNZ 24 Nov 2023" /><ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|implemented on 25 September 2024,<ref name="auto"/>}}
*Restore balance to the school history curriculum.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Combating truancy through enforcement action, data collection, and publishing school attendance data.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Improve the cost-effectiveness of [[School lunches in New Zealand|school lunch programmes]].<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}

===Economic===
*Narrow the [[Reserve Bank of New Zealand]]'s mandate to managing price stability and inflation.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|implemented on 13 December 2023,<ref name="The New Zealand Herald"/>}}
*Expanding the [[Inland Revenue Department (New Zealand)|Inland Revenue Department]]'s tax audit capacity.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}} 
*Increase spending on wealth creation and infrastructure development.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Reducing Core Crown expenditure as a proportion of the overall economy.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Tax cuts will be funded by the reprioritisation of government expenditure and revenue gathering rather than a tax on foreign housing buyers.<ref name="1 News new govt" /><ref name="RNZ 24 Nov 2023" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Strengthening the powers of the [[Grocery Commissioner]] and promoting competition in the [[supermarket]] sector.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Prioritising fair trade agreements with export markets including India.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Repeal the Clean Car Discount.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}

===Employment and social services===
*Repeal the [[Fair Pay Agreements Act 2022|Fair Pay Agreements regime]] by Christmas 2023.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|implemented on 14 December 2023,<ref name="Radio New Zealand"/>}} 
*Expand 90-day trials to include all businesses.<ref name=newshub-election /> {{efn|implemented on 21 December 2023,<ref name="rnz.co.nz"/>}} 
*Commit to moderate increases in the minimum wage each year.<ref name=newshub-election /> {{efn|name=pending}}
*Implementing sanctions against beneficiaries who can work but refuse to find work including electronic money management.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Strengthening obligations on Jobseeker beneficiaries to find work including sanctions.<ref name=newshub-election /> {{efn|name=pending}}
*Restricting the number of doctors who can issue medical certificates for health and disability limits.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}

===Firearms===
*Rewriting the [[Arms Act 1983]]. (unfinished)<ref name=newsroom-whichpolicies /><ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Transferring the firearms regulator to a different agency.<ref name=newsroom-whichpolicies />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Reviewing the national Firearms Registry.<ref name=newsroom-whichpolicies /><ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}

===Foreign affairs===
*Ensure a "National Interest Test" is undertaken before New Zealand accepts any agreements from the [[UN]] and [[WHO]] that limit national decision-making and reconfirm that New Zealand's domestic law holds primacy over any international agreements, and by 1 December 2023 reserve against proposed amendments to WHO health regulations.<ref name="newshub coalition agreement" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Recognising Israel's right to self-defence in the [[Gaza war]].<ref name="RNZ Gaza" /><ref name="NZH Gaza" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Supporting a [[two-state solution]] to the [[Israeli–Palestinian conflict]].<ref name="RNZ Gaza" /><ref name="NZH Gaza" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Condemning [[Hamas]] for initiating the Gaza war and rejecting Hamas' role in any future governance of the [[Gaza Strip]].<ref name="Joint Gaza statement">{{cite press release |title=Joint statement – Prime Ministers of New Zealand, Australia and Canada |url=https://www.beehive.govt.nz/release/joint-statement-prime-ministers-new-zealand-australia-and-canada |website=Beehive.govt.nz |publisher=[[New Zealand Government]] |access-date=21 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231219024801/https://www.beehive.govt.nz/release/joint-statement-prime-ministers-new-zealand-australia-and-canada |archive-date=19 December 2023 |date=13 December 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref>{{efn|name=pending}}
*Designating the whole of Hamas as a terrorist entity, after its military was described this way in 2010.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.beehive.govt.nz/release/nz-designates-entirety-hamas-terrorist-entity |title=NZ designates entirety of Hamas as terrorist entity |date=29 February 2024 |website=Beehive.govt.nz|publisher=[[New Zealand Government]]|access-date=29 February 2024}}</ref>{{efn|name=pending}}
**Designating both [[Hezbollah]] and the [[Houthis]] as terrorist entities.<ref>{{cite news |title=Government designates Hezbollah as terrorist entity |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/political/534333/government-designates-hezbollah-as-terrorist-entity |access-date=21 November 2024 |work=[[RNZ]] |date=20 November 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241121023755/https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/political/534333/government-designates-hezbollah-as-terrorist-entity |archive-date=21 November 2024}}</ref>
*Introducing new legislation to criminalise covert and other subversive foreign interference activities.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Pennington |first1=Phil |title=Bill to stop foreign interference 'undermining core New Zealand interests' introduced to Parliament |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/political/533983/bill-to-stop-foreign-interference-undermining-core-new-zealand-interests-introduced-to-parliament |access-date=16 November 2024 |work=[[RNZ]] |date=16 November 2024}}</ref>

===Health===
*Disestablish the [[Te Aka Whai Ora]] (Māori Health Authority).<ref name=1news-treaty />{{efn|implemented on 28 February 2024,<ref name="Whakaata Māori"/>}}
*Repeal the [[Smokefree Environments and Regulated Products (Smoked Tobacco) Amendment Act 2022]].<ref name="newshub coalition agreement" />{{efn|implemented on 28 February 2024,<ref name="Smokefree generation law scrapped b"/>}}
*Repeal the Therapeutic Products Act 2023.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Review the [[University of Auckland]]'s [[Māori people|Māori]] and [[Pasifika New Zealanders|Pacific]] Admission Scheme and [[University of Otago]] equivalent.<ref name=1news-treaty /><ref name="newshub coalition agreement" /><ref>{{cite news |last1=Stewart |first1=Ella |title=Health Minister Shane Reti responsible for review of 'affirmative action' scheme he graduated from in 1980s |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/national/504971/health-minister-shane-reti-responsible-for-review-of-affirmative-action-scheme-he-graduated-from-in-1980s |access-date=20 December 2023 |work=[[Radio New Zealand]] |date=18 December 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231218194926/https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/national/504971/health-minister-shane-reti-responsible-for-review-of-affirmative-action-scheme-he-graduated-from-in-1980s |archive-date=18 December 2023}}</ref>{{efn|name=pending}}
*Allowing the sale of cold medication containing [[pseudoephedrine]].<ref name="newshub coalition agreement" /><ref>{{cite news |last1=Franks |first1=Raphael |title=Pseudoephedrine back on shelves: Seymour's new Govt win |url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/pseudoephedrine-back-on-shelves-act-leader-david-seymours-win-in-new-coalition-government/MRYO2Z56BNDQROYI5DQOL33VQI/ |work=[[The New Zealand Herald]] |date=24 November 2023 |language=en-NZ |access-date=24 November 2023 |archive-date=24 November 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231124045025/https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/pseudoephedrine-back-on-shelves-act-leader-david-seymours-win-in-new-coalition-government/MRYO2Z56BNDQROYI5DQOL33VQI/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
*End all remaining COVID-19 vaccine mandates.<ref name="RNZ 3 Dec 2023" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Establish an independent public inquiry into the handling of the [[COVID-19 pandemic in New Zealand]].<ref name="RNZ 3 Dec 2023" />{{efn|name=pending}}

===Housing and tenancy===
*Restoring interest deductibility for rental properties in various stages between 2023 and 2026 .<ref name=newshub-election /><ref name="1 News new govt" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Allowing local governments to opt out of the previous government's medium density residential standards.<ref name=newsroom-whichpolicies />{{efn|name=pending}}
