*Equipping Corrections officers with body cameras.<ref name="RNZ 24 Nov 2023" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Introducing legislation dealing with "[[sucker punch|coward punching]]".<ref name="RNZ 24 Nov 2023" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*[[Sentencing (Reinstating Three Strikes) Amendment Act 2024|Reintroducing three strikes]].<ref name="newshub coalition agreement">{{cite news |last1=Ensor |first1=Jamie |title=Election 2023 coalition agreement live updates: Christopher Luxon, David Seymour, Winston Peters reveal Government policy, ministers |url= https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2023/11/election-2023-coalition-agreement-live-updates-christopher-luxon-david-seymour-winston-peters-reveal-government-policy-ministers.html |access-date=24 November 2023 |work=[[Newshub]] |date=24 November 2023 |language=en |archive-date=24 November 2023 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20231124005331/https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2023/11/election-2023-coalition-agreement-live-updates-christopher-luxon-david-seymour-winston-peters-reveal-government-policy-ministers.html |url-status=dead }}</ref>{{efn|implemented on 13 December 2024,<ref name="NZH 13 Dec 2024" />}}
*Removing prisoner reduction targets.<ref name="newshub coalition agreement" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Training 500 new police officers within two years.<ref name=newsroom-whichpolicies />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Increase the number of Youth Aid officers.<ref name=newshub-election /> {{efn|name=pending}}
*Boosting funding for community policing including [[Māori Wardens|Māori]] and Pasifika Wardens, Community Patrol New Zealand, and Neighbourhood Watch.<ref name=newshub-election /> {{efn|name=pending}}
*Protect [[freedom of speech]] by ruling out the introduction of hate speech legislation and stop the Law Commission's work on hate speech legislation.<ref name="newshub coalition agreement" />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Boosting funding to the [[Department of Corrections (New Zealand)|Department of Correction]] to raise staffing levels.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Amending the [[Sentencing Act 2002]] and other legislation to ensure tougher consequences for criminals and to emphasise victims' rights.<ref name=newshub-election />{{efn|name=pending}}
*Introducing legislation to make it a specific offence to assault Police and other first responders.<ref name=newshub-election /> {{efn|name=pending}}
